From 7c37ca57ad984be4f5bb92876ad153cc22e7f0e6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeffrey Effendy <jeffreyeffendy@meta.com>
Date: Tue, 23 Dec 2025 10:31:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 29/63] Revert "Delete config_server and device_config" to
 support older images

Summary:
This reverts Google's commit a500d8bde80d2c8c632147136c750a6b067440f2.

There is a boot issue where graphics composer on A12 vendor images could not retrieve display config.

```
2-23 09:18:09.136  4064  4064 F libc    : Fatal signal 11 (SIGSEGV), code 1 (SEGV_MAPERR), fault addr 0x18 in tid 4064 (android.hardwar), pid 4064 (android.hardwar)
...
12-23 09:18:09.202  4452  4452 F DEBUG   : backtrace:
12-23 09:18:09.202  4452  4452 F DEBUG   :       #00 pc 0000000000006da0  /vendor/lib64/libcuttlefish_device_config_proto.so (cuttlefish::DeviceConfig::DeviceConfig(cuttlefish::DeviceConfig const&)+72) (BuildId: ba7d059f859610113d62e5ce82be2b23)
12-23 09:18:09.202  4452  4452 F DEBUG   :       #01 pc 00000000000024fc  /vendor/lib64/libcuttlefish_device_config.so (cuttlefish::GetDeviceConfig()+52) (BuildId: a982d84a38bc40d7f9dbcf4b28619494)
12-23 09:18:09.203  4452  4452 F DEBUG   :       #02 pc 000000000002c9e4  /vendor/lib64/hw/hwcomposer.ranchu.so (android::findDisplays(std::__1::vector<android::DisplayMultiConfigs, std::__1::allocator<android::DisplayMultiConfigs> >&)+84) (BuildId: 3cbcd16dd3e12422f5cc236f06bef471)
...
```

In A16, display config information is passed via DRM device, however A12 vendor images do graphics composer do not have DRM client to read from the device. See this code reference where [display config is read in A12 by calling GetDeviceInfo](https://www.internalfb.com/code/aosp-device-generic-goldfish-opengl/[smartglasses-12.0%3Ad2e0ffa2e29fb08e46b3a567c1f279766751e599]/system/hwc2/DisplayFinder.cpp?lines=38) and in [A14 where DRM support is added](https://www.internalfb.com/code/aosp-device-generic-goldfish-opengl/[nucleus-14.0%3Ae00f12f71d5553c06aa659586a1daa80f8fc03b0]/system/hwc3/DisplayFinder.cpp?lines=259). And then this is removed eventually in [this commit](https://www.internalfb.com/phabricator/commit/AOSPDEVICEGOOGLECUTTLEFISH/a500d8bde80d2c8c632147136c750a6b067440f2).

So, in order to support older images, we still need to keep `config_server` and `device_config` so the older vendor still able to retrieve display config. This should not affect newer images as they are using `drm` by default.

Test Plan:
**Test on `greatwhite_cf_emu_arm64`**

Steps to run `greatwhite_cf_emu_arm64`: P2094633633

Logcat before: P2094295955
Logcat after: P2094419838

**Test on `tiki_cf_emu_arm64`**

Same step as device, except use this as handle to download tiki image `GICWmAD6BUrXxp4HALFK81Rzn9N-bpd0AAAe` and do not set `--noset_fstab_suffix`

It is booting on tiki
https://pxl.cl/8DpQ2

